ing flippers to a running race would be absurd.","example_zh":"穿著潛水蛙鞋參加跑步比賽會很荒謬。","image_url":"https://jbspxqebcrkilfcddluo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/word-illustrations/senior/absurd-01-v1.webp","local_path":"/images/vocabulary/senior/absurd-01-v1.webp","style":"generated-senior-v1","version":1},{"id":"senior-abundance-01-v1","level":"senior","word":"abundance","sort_order":1,"sense":"豐富","alt_zh":"高中生在花園收成滿滿幾籃番茄，藤上仍結滿成熟果實。","example":"The garden produced an abundance of tomatoes this summer.","example_zh":"今年夏天，花園盛產番茄。","image_url":"https://jbspxqebcrkilfcddluo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/word-illustrations/senior/abundance-01-v1.webp","local_path":"/images/vocabulary/senior/abundance-01-v1.webp","style":"generated-senior-v1","version":1},{"id":"senior-accessible-01-v1","level":"senior","word":"accessible","sort_order":1,"sense":"可進入的；可使用的","alt_zh":"使用輪椅的高中生和朋友沿平緩坡道進入圖書館。","example":"The new ramp made the library accessible to students who use wheelchairs.","example_zh":"新坡道讓使用輪椅的學生也能方便進入圖書館。","image_url":"https://jbspxqebcrkilfcddluo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/word-illustrations/senior/accessible-01-v1.webp","local_path":"/images/vocabulary/senior/accessible-01-v1.webp","style":"generated-senior-v1","version":1},{"id":"senior-adverse-01-v1","level":"senior","word":"adverse","sort_order":1,"sense":"不利的","alt_zh":"山路風雨加劇，登山者轉身沿安全路線下山。","example":"Adverse weather forced the hikers to turn back before reaching the summit.","example_zh":"惡劣天氣迫使登山者在登頂前折返。","image_url":"https://jbspxqebcrkilfcddluo.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/word-illustrations/senior/adverse-01-v1.webp","local_path":"/images/vocabulary/senior/adverse-01-v1.webp","style":"generated-senior-v1","version":1},{"id":"senior-advocate-01-v1","level":"senior","word":"advocate","sort_order":1,"sense":"提倡","alt_zh":"高中生在海邊向大家介紹減塑，展示海龜與可重複使用水瓶的圖示。","example":"The students advocate protecting sea turtles by reducing plastic waste.","example_zh":"學生們提倡減少塑膠垃圾，以保護海龜。","image_url"